.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 29, 2026
.Dt ACCEPT 2
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm accept ,
.Nm accept4
.Nd accept a connection on a socket
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/socket.h
.Ft int
.Fn accept "int s" "struct sockaddr *restrict addr" "socklen_t *restrict addrlen"
.Ft int
.Fo accept4
.Fa "int s"
.Fa "struct sockaddr *restrict addr"
.Fa "socklen_t *restrict addrlen"
.Fa "int flags"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn accept
system call takes the oldest connection from the queue of the listening
socket
.Fa s
.Po
see
.Xr listen 2
.Pc
and returns a new descriptor for it, the lowest one free.
The new socket has the domain, type and protocol of
.Fa s .
It does not inherit
.Dv O_NONBLOCK
or any option of
.Fa s .
.Pp
If
.Fa addr
and
.Fa addrlen
are not
.Dv NULL ,
the peer's address is stored at
.Fa addr ,
at most
.Fa *addrlen
bytes of it, and
.Fa *addrlen
is set to the address's full length.
.Pp
With no connection queued,
.Fn accept
blocks, or fails with
.Er EAGAIN
if
.Fa s
is non-blocking.
A blocking
.Fn accept
waits at most as long as the
.Dv SO_RCVTIMEO
option of
.Fa s
says, if it is set.
A listening socket is readable for
.Xr poll 2
and
.Xr select 2
when a connection is queued.
.Pp
.Fn accept4
is
.Fn accept
with
.Fa flags ,
the OR of none or more of
.Dv SOCK_CLOEXEC
and
.Dv SOCK_NONBLOCK ,
which set the close-on-exec flag on the new descriptor and
.Dv O_NONBLOCK
on the new open file description.
.Pp
If no descriptor can be allocated, the connection stays queued.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
These calls return the new descriptor.
Otherwise they return \-1 and set
.Va errno .
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EAGAIN
The socket is non-blocking and no connection is queued, or
.Dv SO_RCVTIMEO
expired first.
.It Bq Er EBADF
.Fa s
is not an open descriptor.
.It Bq Er ECONNREFUSED
The TCP connection was reset between its arrival and its acceptance.
.It Bq Er EINTR
A signal interrupted the call.
Without a time-out, a handler installed with
.Dv SA_RESTART
restarts it instead.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
The local socket is not listening, or
.Fa flags
holds a flag other than
.Dv SOCK_CLOEXEC
and
.Dv SOCK_NONBLOCK .
.It Bq Er ENFILE
The system limit on open files,
.Va kern.maxfiles ,
has been reached.
.It Bq Er ENOTSOCK
.Fa s
is not a socket.
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
The socket's type does not accept connections, or the TCP socket is not
listening.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bind 2 ,
.Xr connect 2 ,
.Xr listen 2 ,
.Xr socket 2 ,
.Xr unix 4
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Fn accept
system call conforms to
.St -p1003.1-2008 .
.Fn accept4
is in IEEE Std 1003.1-2024.
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn accept
system call first appeared in
.Bx 4.2 ,
and
.Fn accept4
in Linux and
.Fx 10.0 .
In OxideBSD they are system calls 147 and 582.
